extends RefCounted
## The deer, drawn pixel by pixel from the reference the user gave (2026-11-21; the project
## library's survivium-builds/animals/anim/deer/ has it cut into frames and the review of every
## state, anim/src/ the tools that drew from it, HANDOFF.md how), at 0.7 of the reference, the
## scale the user set for every animal (2026-11-21). tools/make_sprites.gd saves it as
## the deer bundle's picture (content/animals/deer/sprites/creatures/deer.png), the sheet
## Creatures draws from.
## The frames as letters (deer_a.py) and this table's writer (write_deer_art.py) are in tools/art/animals/.
##
## Each state has four frames (the user's rule: at most four) for the south (as it comes at the
## camera), the north (as it goes away) and the west; the east is the west mirrored, as the game
## draws it (the reference's east is the west mirrored too, only its spots placed otherwise).
## `idle`: the reference's four frames, the head dipping a pixel and rising. `walk`: the step,
## the reference's frames 1, 2, 4 and 5 of six (as the boar's and the fox's). `run`: the gallop,
## the reference's 1, 3, 5 and 6 of six: legs spread, tucked under,
## pushing off, stretched in the leap. `hurt`: the flinch at a blow, the reference's four: struck, the head
## ducked, pressed down, ducked. `death`: the reference's frames 2, 4, 5 and 7 of seven: struck, falling,
## flat on the ground, lying dead; the game keeps the last until its carcass is taken
## (the user's rule). Hurt and death are in the deer's own colours, though the reference paints
## them red: the game flashes a struck animal red with a shader (the user, 2026-11-21).
##
## A frame is rows of letters of INK ("." empty), the outline drawn as letters too. The frames of
## a view share one canvas, so the body does not jump between states; its last row is the ground
## (the reference's ground row of every frame lands on it, the lying deer's too).

## The colours of the letters: the outline and the darkest (K k O o D), the fur from dark to light
## (d M m L l H), its grey-brown shade (h F) and the cream of the spots, the throat and the belly
## (T t W E e).
