## canvases' height. Each view's canvas stands on the cell's last row.
const CELL := Vector2i(28, 21)
## The column of each view's canvas over the animal's place, the cell's middle (the game puts that
## on it and mirrors the side about it): the side's between the standing feet, so the body keeps its
## place as it turns about and only the head and the tail swap sides; the front's and the back's in
## the middle, between the legs.
const MIDDLE := {"w": 14, "s": 5, "n": 5}
